The upstream project does not ship the DSH integration as a separate package;
it is compiled into the main `@agentmemory/agentmemory` bundle.

Modifications (Apache-2.0 section 4(b) — STATEMENT OF CHANGES)
--------------------------------------------------------------
File: lib/index.js (derived from dist/integrations/dsh.mjs @ 0.9.33)

  1. 2026-11-02 — Remote plain-HTTP daemons are accepted.
     The URL guard in post() originally rejected any non-loopback `http://`
     endpoint even when an explicit bearer secret was configured:
         ... || secret && target.protocol !== "https:" && !isLoopbackUrl(url)
     That clause was removed. Licensed under the same terms as upstream.

  2. 2026-11-10 — Injected memory gets its own size ceiling.
     `safe()` defaults to an 8000-character cap that exists for captured tool
     output. The `/context` and `/session/start` response bodies are injected
     memory, not capture output, and were being truncated mid-sentence once
     the daemon's pinned memory slots exceeded 8000 characters.
     Added `contextMaxChars(config)` — default 64000, overridable via the
     plugin's `contextMaxChars` config key or the
     AGENTMEMORY_CONTEXT_MAX_CHARS environment variable — and passed it at
     both call sites. The default 8000 cap on captured tool output is
     unchanged.

  3. 2026-11-14 — Removed the dangling `//# sourceMappingURL=dsh.mjs.map`
     trailer, since the source map is not part of this package.

Both source patches are marked inline with `PATCHED 2026-11-02` and
`PATCHED 2026-11-10` comments so they stay visible.

